schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: GG24 Bioregional Reforestation Round scale
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    In GG24 (the round Gitcoin ran October 14-28, 2025 as the first round of
    its "Gitcoin 3.0" relaunch), the Bioregional Reforestation Round carried a
    $100,000 matching pool spread across nine bioregions, including Nigeria,
    Kenya/Uganda, Cascadia, and the Mediterranean Coast, with roughly 1,286
    unique donors making about 3,042 donations, and co-funders including
    CeloPG, the Ethereum Foundation, the Climate Coordination Network, and
    the BioFi Project.
  evidence: >-
    Cited in the article's References to "Gitcoin Grants 24 (GG24)"
    (https://gitcoin.co/campaigns/gitcoin-grants-24-gg24) and "Bioregional
    Reforestation Round" (https://gov.gitcoin.co/t/bioregional-reforestation-round/24927).
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/gitcoin-grants-qf.md
  interpretation: >-
    Used in the article as proof that quadratic funding already routes real
    money to on-the-ground regenerative work, not just crypto infrastructure
    — offered as the concrete case a local node running tree-planting, food
    sovereignty, or watershed work could look to.
  uncertainty: >-
    Donor/donation counts are approximate ("roughly," "about") as reported in
    the article's cited sources; not independently re-verified for this
    ingestion.
  high_risk: true
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/gitcoin-grants-qf.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
